✨ Features

RunCard lifecycle – create, edit and progress instruction cards step‑by‑step

Digital signatures – workers sign each stage before moving forward

Role‑based access control (RBAC) – admins, supervisors, operators

Audit trail – every action is logged for traceability

Responsive UI – works on desktop, tablet and shop‑floor terminals


🛠️ Tech Stack

Layer	Technology

Backend	C# / ASP.NET MVC, Entity Framework
Database	SQL Server
Frontend	JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3
Dev Ops	Docker & Docker Compose, GitHub Actions
Testing	xUnit + FluentAssertions (unit) • Playwright (E2E)


🗂️ Architecture

┌───────────┐      ┌────────┐      ┌────────────┐
│   UI      │      │  BLL   │      │    DAL     │
│ (MVC + JS)│──▶──▶│ Services│──▶──▶│ EF Models  │
└───────────┘      └────────┘      └────────────┘
        ▲                               │
        │ REST API                      │ SQL
        ▼                               ▼
    Client App                    SQL Server

> Separation of Concerns: the Business Logic Layer (BLL) orchestrates workflow rules, while the Data Access Layer (DAL) owns all queries.



⚡ Local Setup

# clone repository
$ git clone https://github.com/nadav770/CardVirtual.git
$ cd CardVirtual

# run inside Visual Studio *or* with Docker (recommended)
$ docker compose up --build -d  # http://localhost:8080

🐳 Docker Compose

version: '3.9'
services:
  app:
    build: .
    ports:
      - "8080:80"
    environment:
      - ConnectionStrings__Default=Server=db;Database=CardVirtual;User=sa;Password=Your_strong_password123;
    depends_on:
      - db
  db:
    image: mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest
    environment:
      - ACCEPT_EULA=Y
      - SA_PASSWORD=Your_strong_password123
    ports:
      - "1433:1433"

🧪 Running Tests

# unit tests
$ dotnet test
# E2E tests (Playwright)
$ npx playwright test

🚀 CI / CD

A reusable GitHub Actions pipeline (<code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code>) builds the project, runs tests, publishes a Docker image and can deploy to Azure Web App / Render / Fly.io.

name: CI
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v4
        with:
          dotnet-version: "8.0.x"
      - name: Restore
        run: dotnet restore
      - name: Build
        run: dotnet build --no-restore --configuration Release
      - name: Test
        run: dotnet test --no-build --configuration Release --logger trx
      - name: Publish Docker image
        uses: docker/build-push-action@v5
        with:
          context: .
          push: true
          tags: your-dockerhub-user/cardvirtual:latest

